WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.924
Morning, Ziad.

00:00:00.924 --> 00:00:02.310
Saturday the seventh.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:07.127
A hard one to start, a wide open afternoon, and a party on there tonight.

00:00:07.127 --> 00:00:09.569
Here's one to chew on while you move.

00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:13.726
On a bumpy city street, why can a rock-hard tire end up slower?

00:00:13.726 --> 00:00:15.046
Answer's at the end.

00:00:15.046 --> 00:00:16.960
Weather's a little unsettled.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:25.868
A shower or two could pass through this morning and maybe one more in the afternoon, nothing steady, breezy, and up to the mid-sixties.

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:28.706
I couldn't get exact timing on the showers.

00:00:28.706 --> 00:00:29.630
Okay, the day.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:34.315
Calendar has four by four intervals at seven, about forty-five minutes.

00:00:34.315 --> 00:00:36.559
There's a birthday on there today.

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:43.026
And a surprise party for it is on the calendar from seven to ten tonight, still marked as a maybe.

00:00:43.026 --> 00:00:45.072
Everything in between is yours.

00:00:45.072 --> 00:00:45.996
Alright, news.

00:00:45.996 --> 00:00:46.986
Just two today.

00:00:46.986 --> 00:00:50.879
Wall Street had a rough Thursday, and it was all about A.I.

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:58.072
The big tech index fell more than six percent in a day, wiping out a record two point three trillion dollars.

00:00:58.072 --> 00:01:02.889
Chip stocks dropped about twelve percent, and Nvidia lost more than nine.

00:01:02.889 --> 00:01:09.093
The worry is that the new Democratic Congress slows down all those giant data center projects.

00:01:09.093 --> 00:01:11.666
By Friday the slide had mostly stopped.

00:01:11.666 --> 00:01:15.626
Still, it shows how much of the market is riding on one bet.

00:01:15.626 --> 00:01:18.991
And one that touches anyone who puts photos online.

00:01:18.991 --> 00:01:27.108
OpenAI, Google, Microsoft, and Anthropic are backing one shared signal that a website can use to say, don't train your A.I.

00:01:27.108 --> 00:01:27.900
on my stuff.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:33.179
Right now every company has its own rules, so opting out means chasing each one.

00:01:33.179 --> 00:01:41.164
Separately, Meta hit pause on a plan to scrape sites run by its business users, after court rulings in Norway and Brazil.

00:01:41.164 --> 00:01:44.596
None of this pulls back what's already been scraped.

00:01:44.596 --> 00:01:50.799
But a single off switch would be a real step for anyone whose portfolio lives on the open web.

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:53.570
Okay, here's the main thing for this week.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:02:01.093
Tuesday at seven, a place called Sprout Society, on Scott Avenue in Bushwick, runs something called The Sing Easy.

00:02:01.093 --> 00:02:04.921
It's a guided group singing session, about eighty minutes.

00:02:04.921 --> 00:02:09.474
Tickets run roughly fifteen to thirty-five bucks, on a sliding scale.

00:02:09.474 --> 00:02:14.490
Nobody's performing, and you don't need to read music or think you can sing.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:22.738
A voice teacher walks the room through breathing, some goofy vocal play, and a few simple songs everybody learns on the spot.

00:02:22.738 --> 00:02:27.820
The whole point is the sound of a room full of people getting loose together.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.931
It fits you more than it sounds.

00:02:29.931 --> 00:02:36.465
You've spent the last few weeks picking a voice for this memo, so here's a chance to work your own.

00:02:36.465 --> 00:02:42.536
It's a short ride from home, and Tuesday's a good night to do something that isn't a screen.

00:02:42.536 --> 00:02:50.917
And if you want an easy food plan this weekend, there's a new Persian spot called Azar opening in Williamsburg right about now.

00:02:50.917 --> 00:02:53.226
Today's challenge is for your body.

00:02:53.226 --> 00:03:00.287
Sometime today, when you're carrying something, bags, a gift for tonight, groceries, carry it the long way.

00:03:00.287 --> 00:03:07.348
Arms straight down, shoulders back and down, stand tall, and walk like you're not carrying anything at all.

00:03:07.348 --> 00:03:09.262
It's called a farmer's carry.

00:03:09.262 --> 00:03:10.780
A few blocks is plenty.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:22.328
It works your grip, your back, and your core all at once, and it's the kind of strength that shows up everywhere, from lifting a bike up the stairs to holding a camera steady.

00:03:22.328 --> 00:03:27.014
Okay, something new today, and it's one for the run you're probably on.

00:03:27.014 --> 00:03:29.389
Why intervals tend to come in fours.

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:33.019
The four by four setup comes out of research in Norway.

00:03:33.019 --> 00:03:36.714
Four minutes hard, about three minutes easy, four times.

00:03:36.714 --> 00:03:43.115
In one well-known study, people doing it for eight weeks noticeably raised their top-end fitness.

00:03:43.115 --> 00:03:48.131
People doing the same total work at a steady, moderate pace barely moved it.

00:03:48.131 --> 00:03:50.638
The reason is how your heart ramps up.

00:03:50.638 --> 00:03:55.852
When you start a hard effort, your heart rate doesn't jump straight to the top.

00:03:55.852 --> 00:03:57.831
It climbs for a minute or two.

00:03:57.831 --> 00:04:01.593
So a short sprint ends before your heart ever gets there.

00:04:01.593 --> 00:04:06.938
Four minutes is long enough to spend a couple of those minutes close to your max.

00:04:06.938 --> 00:04:08.852
That's the zone that matters.

00:04:08.852 --> 00:04:14.197
Near max, your heart is pushing out the most blood it can with every single beat.

00:04:14.197 --> 00:04:18.223
Spend enough time there, over and over, and the heart adapts.

00:04:18.223 --> 00:04:20.928
It gets stronger and pumps more per beat.

00:04:20.928 --> 00:04:25.218
That's a big part of what fitness people mean by a bigger engine.

00:04:25.218 --> 00:04:27.725
The easy jog in between is clever too.

00:04:27.725 --> 00:04:32.939
It's long enough to let your legs recover, so the next round can be hard again.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:37.690
But it's short enough that your heart rate never drops all the way down.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:44.685
So the next rep gets you back up to the top faster, and you get more good minutes out of the same workout.

00:04:44.685 --> 00:04:48.644
That's also why the rest of the week is supposed to be easy.

00:04:48.644 --> 00:04:52.340
The hard days only pay off if you show up to them fresh.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:56.827
So: calendar says intervals at seven and the party at seven tonight.

00:04:56.827 --> 00:04:58.411
And try that long carry.

00:04:58.411 --> 00:05:04.218
The answer: the bumps jolt you and the bike instead of the tire, and that energy's gone.

00:05:04.218 --> 00:05:06.000
Have a good Saturday, Ziad.
